# PROBE (POST-M8A-COMMON-INEFFICIENCY-CENSUS.md, supporting evidence only):
# bench/refined-checks.ir with its one non-ASCII literal replaced by an
# ASCII string of IDENTICAL per-character control flow through Emailish?'s
# scanners -- "cafe@ab.xyz" vs "café@例え.テスト": local part 4 alnum chars,
# "@", one 2-char alpha label, ".", a 3-char alpha TLD, 11 characters in
# both -- so every scanner takes the same branches the same number of
# times. The instruction difference between the two profiles is exactly
# the cost of the non-ASCII representation path (UTF-8 re-seek from byte 0
# per region access, Unicode decoding, Unicode class tables).
# bench/refined-checks.ir itself is not modified.
# Repeated refined-type predicates: an outer Emailish? check whose result is
# re-checked in the then branch (statically redundant), and UriQueryValue?
# on a value whose type proves the answer.
#
# The first check's string is a Unicode-forcing case, not ASCII-only: "é"
# (local part), "例え" (a domain label) and "テスト" (the TLD) are all
# non-ASCII letters that Emailish?'s Tcl-compatible [:alpha:]/[:alnum:]
# classes accept -- see NATIVE-TCL-UNICODE.md. This is deliberate: an
# ASCII-only character-class regression (e.g. Rust's is_ascii_alphanumeric,
# this benchmark's own mistake before this milestone -- see
# bench/equivalents/rust/refined_checks.rs's header) would silently reject
# it, so this benchmark itself now exercises the same Unicode boundary its
# cross-language equivalents must agree on, not only the ASCII happy path.
# requires: web

{bind check
    {block {n acc s q}
        {if {call {ref <=} {ref n} {const 0}}
            {block {} {ref acc}}
            {block {}
                {bind hit
                    {if {call {ref Emailish?} {ref s}}
                        {block {}
                            {if {call {ref Emailish?} {ref s}}
                                {block {} {if {call {ref UriQueryValue?} {ref q}}
                                              {block {} {const 1}}
                                              {block {} {const 0}}}}
                                {block {} {const 0}}}}
                        {block {} {const 0}}}}
                {call {ref check}
                    {call {ref -} {ref n} {const 1}}
                    {call {ref +} {ref acc} {ref hit}}
                    {ref s}
                    {ref q}}}}}}

{bind q {call {ref uriEscape} {const str {a b}}}}

{call {ref list}
    {call {ref check} {const 400} {const 0} {const str cafe@ab.xyz} {ref q}}
    {call {ref check} {const 400} {const 0} {const str not-an-email} {ref q}}}
